# SfxLab family v2: layer id name type dur seed key=value... (dur 0 = endless) · range id param lo hi [note] · bind signal id|* param [lo hi] [rel] [steps=N | scale=<chord>] · note text · then `spell <id>` sections: name, recipe, the spell's layers at their lock values, its binds and notes
bench 1
root 65.4064
# aqueous_mystic — the aqueous plan bent away from the real thing. Same recordings, same subtraction (four bandpasses at the chord
# tones, levels from tone.*), but nothing plays at the speed it was recorded: the surface runs at a third to nine tenths of real
# time (keep-len, the pen's speed), the note copies are slowed an octave in tape mode (big slow drops), the rumble is stretched
# and cleaned of its inharmonics (an underwater organ). The filters ring harder (resonance 0.9-0.97) and the notes echo. The
# droplets (the stream's partials, always gathered onto the chord, shimmering) grow with the machine and FREEZE as the ratios
# come in tune: at coherence 1 the water stands still (spectral freeze). Reverbs wide, echo on the drips.
layer bed aqueous/Aqueous_underwater_rumbling_00001 7 0.0000 5001 level=0.60000 attack=1.20000 release=1.80000 pitch=4.42000 pitch_swp=0.00000 cutoff=0.50000 cutoff_swp=0.00000 resonance=0.00000 filter=0.00000 pan=0.00000 pan_swp=0.00000 echo=0.00000 drive=0.10000 start=0.00000 speed=0.70000 sines=1.00000 residual=0.60000 floor=14.00000 min_len=46.00000 loop=1.00000 odd/even=0.00000 tilt=0.00000 purity=0.30000 stretch=0.04000 gather=0.00000 chord=1.00000 shimmer=0.00000 root_shift=0.00000 harm_tol=3.00000 lfo_rate=4.00000 lfo>pitch=0.00000 lfo>cut=0.00000 lfo>amp=0.00000 lfo_shape=0.00000 env_curve=0.00000 reverb=0.45000 flange=0.00000 flange_fb=0.50000 duck=0.00000 duck_from=0.00000 phaser=0.00000 phaser_rate=0.40000 ph_stages=4.00000 ph_pos=-1.00000 lfo_pos=-1.00000 flange_pos=-1.00000 file=aqueous/Aqueous_underwater_rumbling_00001.ogg keyed=1
