range bed level 0.3 0.6 the rumble as an underwater organ: stretched to 0.7x, inharmonics faded (purity 0.3), a little bell stretch
range surface level 0 0.35 the stream in slow motion (0.35x .. 0.9x of real time, the pen's speed), flanged, echoing
range surface speed 0.35 0.9 never real time
range surface flange_pos 0 1 the comb's delay, parked by the orb's curl (the mix is fixed at 0.4)
range root level 0 0.45 the root: the stream slowed an octave (tape) through a bandpass at C4 that rings (resonance 0.9-0.97 from fit), echoing
range root resonance 0.9 0.97
range third level 0 0.4 E4
range fifth level 0 0.4 G4
range seventh level 0 0.3 Bb4
range droplets level 0 1 the droplets, always gathered onto the chord, shimmering: grow with the machine
range droplets speed 0.05 1 time itself: real at coherence 0, all but frozen (spectral freeze) at coherence 1
bind stir bed level 0.6 0.4
bind stack bed level 0 -0.12 rel
bind orb.radius bed cutoff 0.35 0.65
bind stir surface level 0 0.35
bind orb.speed surface speed 0.35 0.9
bind orb.curl surface flange_pos 0 1
bind orb.radius surface cutoff 0.5 1
bind tone.root root level 0 0.45
bind tone.third third level 0 0.4
bind tone.fifth fifth level 0 0.4
bind tone.seventh seventh level 0 0.3
bind fit root resonance 0.9 0.97
bind fit third resonance 0.9 0.97
bind fit fifth resonance 0.9 0.97
bind fit seventh resonance 0.9 0.97
bind orb.accel root drive 0.08 0.2
bind orb.accel fifth drive 0.08 0.2
bind stack droplets level 0 1
bind coherence droplets speed 1 0.05
bind radiance droplets reverb 0.6 0.95
note aqueous_mystic (draft, 2026-09-27): the aqueous v1 plan with time bent. Compare with aqueous in the family picker; the spells are copies
note of aqueous's (same layer ids), so a spell file can be shared or diverged later. Levers used, in order of how far they take it from
note the recording: droplets speed (freeze with coherence) > note copies an octave down in tape mode > surface keep-len slow motion +
note flange > bed purity/stretch/0.7x > resonance 0.9-0.97 > echo on the notes and the drip > reverbs. All of it is authoring, no new samples.

